WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.820
Now that there's a new Black Panther on the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.900
the balance of power in the MCU is about to&nbsp;
change — in more ways than you might think.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.460
The official trailer for Black Panther: Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever teased it, and the movie has no problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.840
confirming it: There's a new Black Panther&nbsp;
in town, and her name is Shuri. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.680
this is not the playful, happy-go-lucky Shuri&nbsp;
that fans might remember from Black Panther.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.300
Much like her predecessor and brother T'Challa,&nbsp;
she goes through a great deal of loss and sorrow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.040
before fully embracing her role as Wakanda's&nbsp;
protector. Not only does T'Challa himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.660
die unseen in the early stages of the movie,&nbsp;
but Wakanda Forever antagonist Namor's attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.640
ends up killing her mother, Queen Ramonda.
Shuri starts the movie in denial over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.380
spiritual world and the Black Panther tradition,&nbsp;
preferring to focus on science instead. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.940
Ramonda's death and the impending threat of&nbsp;
Namor's Talokan forces cause her to return to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.560
an old project: an artificial recreation of&nbsp;
the Heart-Shaped Herb. With the help of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.060
old research, T'Challa's DNA, and a gift from&nbsp;
Namor, Shuri manages to create a new version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.660
of the plant that gives Black Panthers&nbsp;
their powers — and promptly uses it.
 &nbsp;

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.440
Up until now, the Heart-Shaped Herb&nbsp;
has been treated as a highly unique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.220
commodity that was lost forever when&nbsp;
Killmonger destroyed the remaining crops.&nbsp;

00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:10.427
"Burn it all!"

00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:13.320
Now that Shuri has figured out a way to replicate 

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.340
the precious plant, however, it might have a&nbsp;
huge impact on the Marvel Cinematic Universe.&nbsp;

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.680
Judging by how Shuri manages to go toe-to-toe with&nbsp;
Namor in the finale, it seems that her artificial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.180
Heart-Shaped Herb is comparable to the original,&nbsp;
and seems to be at least as potent as the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.980
prominent superpowered substance in the MCU:&nbsp;
Abraham Erskine's Super Soldier Serum, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:37.800
famously turns Steve Rogers into Captain America.
As it happens, the Super Soldier Serum is a huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.720
deal in the MCU. For decades, scientist after&nbsp;
scientist and nation after nation has tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.340
replicate the effects of Erskine's serum, after&nbsp;
the original recipe was lost with Erskine himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.380
The results of these often dubious experiments&nbsp;
have ranged from Red Skull and the Abomination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.240
to U.S. Agent and the Flag Smashers. So imagine&nbsp;
what will happen when the world finds out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.260
Wakanda is sitting on a substance that can make&nbsp;
people at least as powerful as Captain America.&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.760
The day the world discovers the existence of&nbsp;
Shuri's Heart-Shaped Herb could be nearer than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.600
you'd think, too, because there's one person&nbsp;
outside Wakanda who already knows about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.460
Though Riri Williams doesn't witness the entire&nbsp;
process of recreating the Heart-Shaped Herb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.500
she is present during Shuri's ingestion ritual. As&nbsp;
such, she has a good idea of how the herb is used,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.700
and of the risks involved. What's more,&nbsp;
she specifically requests some for herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.180
after seeing its effects on Shuri.
While that line about wanting to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.860
the herb herself is played as a joke, Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever establishes Riri as a highly intelligent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.540
person with an inquisitive mind. If her rather&nbsp;
obvious gadgeteer genius parallels with Tony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.680
Stark continue, it would be almost surprising&nbsp;
if she didn't end up tinkering with a version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.820
of the recipe, or using her connection with&nbsp;
Shuri to learn more about the new Heart-Shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.260
Herb. She might even inadvertently reveal&nbsp;
its existence to somebody. If that happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.860
or Shuri's new Heart-Shaped Herb recipe&nbsp;
gets out of Wakanda in some other way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.360
the MCU could be looking at a whole new generation&nbsp;
of super soldiers running around the block.

